    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "NE 7, NYJ 3",
        "text": "Jason Sanders' 42-yard field goal put the Jets up 3–0, and Romeo Doubs answered with a diving 42-yard touchdown catch from Drake Maye with 4:10 left. Doubs left after the score with a shoulder injury and did not return."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "NE 17, NYJ 3",
        "text": "Andy Borregales' 32-yard field goal made it 10–3 with 1:46 left, and Maye's 9-yard touchdown pass to DeMario Douglas with 14 seconds left sent New England to halftime up 17–3."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "NE 17, NYJ 13",
        "text": "Omar Cooper Jr. got behind safety Craig Woodson for a 48-yard touchdown from Geno Smith (17–10). David Bailey then stripped TreVeyon Henderson and the Jets took over at the New England 36, but Elijah Ponder's sack held them to Sanders' 36-yard field goal, 17–13 with 4:46 left."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: NE 26, NYJ 19",
        "text": "Maye's 7-yard touchdown pass to Hunter Henry capped a 12-play, 68-yard drive early in the quarter, but Borregales missed the extra point (23–13). Charles Woods intercepted Smith four plays later, Smith's first interception of the season, and the teams traded field goals the rest of the way: Borregales' 27-yarder with 1:12 left made it 26–16 before Sanders' 36-yarder with 32 seconds left."
      }
    ],
